  "sourceFinding": "Same RootView layout and BoardMapView animation code executes in both same-binary arms: paired-hand insertion changes available board height, aspect-fit scales board; highlightedHoldIDs drives easeInOut(.18). Projection flag only changes hand camera projection, not these layout declarations. This does not establish identical scheduling or a continuous measured .18-second animation.",
  "prospectiveRuleForRemainingP2O2": {
    "requiresParentApproval": true,
    "scope": "Additional explicitly named observed endpoint/path correspondence; do not replace original exact-set checker or retroactively mark it passed.",
    "endpointEquality": "Require exact initial and settled endpoint tuples equal to both recorded controls; same board root/camera/layout viewport endpoint values, same actual matching ARView identity within each run.",
    "path": "Every observed matching board ARView frame must lie on A+lambda*(B-A), lambda within[0,1], observed lambda nondecreasing. Use at most1e-5 point component residual solely for floating serialization arithmetic, far below a layout unit. Do not use bounding-box or pixel tolerance to hide geometry changes.",
    "semanticWindow": "All non-endpoint samples must occur only during the first active-selection startup transition and strictly before the first screenshot command starts. Require B at the first complete board census after that screenshot ends, with that observation no later than the second(+1s) screenshot command end. All later observed board frames through the final tail must remain exactly B. If any of these conditions fails, stop/review; no compensating frames or further heuristic extension.",
    "unchangedGates": "Preserve all existing CPU brackets, complete trace/tail, actual camera/clip facts, lifecycle order/counts, source/binary/package parity, all whole-image judgments and phase timing gates. No source/validator/runtime edits by this audit.",
    "why": "Set equality compares time-sampled animation positions from different offsets; endpoint/path/window correspondence tests geometric layout equivalence at the resolution actually observed. It deliberately does not claim temporal equivalence."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Original control-correspondence boardFrames=false remains an honest historical failure.",
    "The two intermediate records occur before first screenshot start, but neither trace observes B until AFTER the first screenshot ends. First screenshot settlement is not proven.",
    "Sparse observations cannot prove continuous affine motion between records, equal easing/duration, identical presentation transaction scheduling or lack of overshoot between samples.",
    "Same source and binary do not exclude projection-dependent timing effects. The prospective rule accepts that timing confound explicitly and cannot by itself establish a rendering fix or causality.",
    "No screenshot pixel measurement or image manipulation; all arithmetic uses raw UIKit census tuples. No source/runtime/validator modifications."
  ]
}
